Using Bit Manipulation -  O(n*(2^n)) Time and O(n*(2^n)) SpaceThe idea is to generate the i-th Gray code directly using the formula: Gray(i) = i ^ (i >> 1) , where ^ represents the bitwise XOR operator.We iterate through all numbers from 0 to 2^n - 1 and compute the corresponding Gray code using the above formula. Each generated Gray code is then converted into an n-bit binary string and added to the result.For n = 3, we generate the Gray codes by iterating from 0 to 2^3 - 1 = 7 and applying the formula:  Gray(i) = i ^ (i >> 1)The generated Gray codes are:Gray(0) = 0 ^ 0 = 0   -> 000Gray(1) = 1 ^ 0 = 1   -> 001Gray(2) = 2 ^ 1 = 3   -> 011Gray(3) = 3 ^ 1 = 2   -> 010Gray(4) = 4 ^ 2 = 6   -> 110Gray(5) = 5 ^ 2 = 7   -> 111Gray(6) = 6 ^ 3 = 5   -> 101Gray(7) = 7 ^ 3 = 4   -> 100Thus, the generated 3-bit Gray code sequence is: 000 001 011 010 110 111 101 100
